<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<pnml xmlns="http://www.pnml.org/version-2009/grammar/pnml">
  <net id="SEQ-15b" type="http://www.pnml.org/version-2009/grammar/ptnet">
    <name><text>15b Transfer of funds from one agency to another body that will implement</text></name>
    <page id="page1">
      <place id="p1"><name><text>start</text></name><initialMarking><text>1</text></initialMarking></place>
      <place id="p2"><name><text>p2</text></name></place>
      <place id="p3"><name><text>p3</text></name></place>
      <place id="p4"><name><text>p4</text></name></place>
      <place id="p5"><name><text>p5</text></name></place>
      <place id="p6"><name><text>p6</text></name></place>
      <place id="p7"><name><text>p7</text></name></place>
      <place id="p8"><name><text>p8</text></name></place>
      <place id="p9"><name><text>p9</text></name></place>
      <place id="p10"><name><text>p10</text></name></place>
      <place id="p11"><name><text>p11</text></name></place>
      <place id="p12"><name><text>p12</text></name></place>
      <place id="p13"><name><text>p13</text></name></place>
      <place id="p14"><name><text>p14</text></name></place>
      <place id="p15"><name><text>end</text></name></place>
      <transition id="t01"><name><text>1. National agency to Implementing body: Memorandum of agreement: purpose, amount (enough for three months, or the total project cost), period, reports</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t02"><name><text>2. National agency: Obligation recorded against its own allotment</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t03"><name><text>3. National agency to Implementing body: Check in the name of the implementing body. The receiver issues an official receipt</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t04"><name><text>4. National agency: Books: Due from National Government Agencies (a receivable). Not yet an expense, not yet a disbursement in the budget reports</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t05"><name><text>5. Implementing body: Trust fund books: Due to NGAs (a liability). The money goes to a trust account, or to the Treasury, from which DBM gives an NCA for trust</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t06"><name><text>6. Implementing body to Suppliers and payees: Procurement, contract</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t07"><name><text>7. Suppliers and payees to Implementing body: Delivery, inspected and accepted</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t08"><name><text>8. Implementing body to Suppliers and payees: Payment from the trust account or under the NCA for trust</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t09"><name><text>9. Implementing body to National agency: Within ten days after each month: reports of checks issued and of cash disbursements, approved by the head of the implementing body</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t10"><name><text>10. National agency: Books: expense recorded, receivable reduced. Now reported as disbursed. The implementing body reduces its liability by the same expenses</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="tau1"><name><text>skip: Money remains at the end of the project or of the validity period</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t11"><name><text>11. Implementing body to National agency: Unused balance returned, if the agreement says so</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="tau2"><name><text>end of: Money remains at the end of the project or of the validity period</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t12"><name><text>12. National agency to DBM: FAR 1-C each quarter: obligations, disbursements, liquidations and balances of fund transfers</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t13"><name><text>13. COA to National agency: The auditor of the implementing body audits its payments. The auditor of the source agency audits the transfer</text></name></transition>
